<title>GERMANY: Didier resumes dividend as 96 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Didier resumes dividend as 96 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   18.47   vs 16.52</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share		 7.80    vs 7.00 dmk</p>
<p>    Dividend				     2 marks vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German company is Didier-Werke AG. The manufacturer of blast furnace linings and hot blast stoves last paid a dividend on 1992 results, when it paid four marks. Didier is majority-owned by Austria's Radex-Heraklith AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
